abstract: >
  SIRIUS LOCAL AI is a fully modular, offline-only AI runtime designed for secure,
  deterministic execution of commands, workflows, plugins, and semantic automation.
  Version 5.0.0 introduces the Unified Runtime Architecture, merging PC and Mobile
  logic into a single deterministic, identity-aware, multimodal AI operating layer.

  The Runtime Core 5.0 provides unified orchestration, deterministic execution,
  capability-based access control, and identity-aware routing across all modules.
  AITE 5.0 delivers multimodal semantic triage for text, images, OCR, documents,
  code, and schoolwork, enabling instant and safe routing of all user inputs.

  SECURITY FAMILY 5.0 expands identity and family safety layers with OWNER/FAMILY/
  STRANGER identity levels, time-limits v3, safe-mode for unknown users, and a
  Schoolwork Engine ensuring unrestricted access to academic tasks.

  The system operates entirely on the user's device, without any cloud dependencies
  or external data transmission. All modules follow strict security boundaries,
  deterministic behavior, semantic understanding, and predictable execution rules.

  Version 5.0.0 upgrades the entire runtime stack, including Workflow Engine 5.0,
  Reasoning Engine 5.0, ENVOY 5.0, FS‑AGENT 5.0, CME‑MEM 5.0, System Agent 5.0,
  and Password Vault 5.0. These upgrades prepare the architecture for the upcoming
  Self‑Repair Layer in the 5.x → 6.0 transition.
